title: Text fields and their history
tags: GUI
kind: reference
aliases: text-zones history-zones fields-with-history
summary: Every text field of the GUI: which keep an input history, in which file, and when an entry is recorded; and which keep none.

Which text fields remember what was submitted in them. How to recall it, and how the
history works: [[Input history]]. An entry is never recorded while typing.

!! With a history

''Name'' is the field's name for `history:prev`, `history:next`, `history:search` and for `focus` in a keybinding: `—` means that only `self-focus` reaches it, while it has the focus. ''File'' is under `.metafolder/gui/history/`.

|!Field |!Where |!Name |!File |!Recorded when |
|command input, command mode (`:`) |the shell |— |`shell:command` |a command runs: the one chosen in the list, not the letters typed |
|command input, bash mode (`!`) |the shell |— |`shell:bash` |a line runs |
|the line |[[shell panel]] |`line` |`shell:bash`, shared with the bash mode |a line runs; an answer to a running program is not recorded |
|find bar |the shell ([[Find in a panel]]) |`find`, in a keybinding only |`shell:find` |`Enter` or `Shift+Enter` steps to a match |
|finder |[[metarecord-list panel]] |`finder` |`metarecord-list:finder` |it is applied |
|simplified query |[[metarecord-list panel]] |`simplified` |`metarecord-list:query` |it is applied |
|normal query |[[metarecord-list panel]] |`normal` |`metarecord-list:normal` |it is applied, or a command shows a query there |
|columns |[[metarecord-list panel]] |`columns` |`metarecord-list:columns` |they are applied: as the field then shows them |
|order field |[[metarecord-list panel]] |`order` |`metarecord-list:order` |the order is turned on |
|search box |[[help panel]] |`search` |`help:search` |it is applied |
|intents file |[[sync panel]] |`intents` |`sync:intents` |a plan is asked for |
|filter |[[config panel]] |`filter` |`config:filter` |`Enter` validates it ([[editing:validate]]) |
|filter |[[keybindings-variables panel]] |`filter` |`keybindings-variables:filter` |`Enter` validates it ([[editing:validate]]) |
|key of the form |[[keybindings panel]] |`key` |`keybindings:key` |`Enter` validates it, or the line is saved |
|command of the form |[[keybindings panel]] |`command` |`keybindings:command` |`Enter` validates it, or the line is saved |

`Escape`, or clicking elsewhere, records nothing in any of them.

!! Without a history

|!Field |!Where |
|command input, answering a question: a command's argument, a script's prompt |the shell ([[Interactive command arguments]]) |
|search box of `history:search` |the shell |
|link hints |the shell |
|renaming a workspace |the tab bar |
|field name and value of the bulk edit |[[metarecord-list panel]] |
|field name to add, and a field's value when adding or editing it |`metarecord-detail` panel |
|name and root of a new repository, root to load, field name to retype |`repos` panel |
|text being edited |[[viewer panel]] |
|key of each row |[[keybindings panel]] |
|value of each variable |[[keybindings-variables panel]] |

The expansion of the simplified query in [[metarecord-list panel]] is read-only: nothing is typed there.
